I wrote the plan for two tasks, plus the issue responses. The commit step did nothing: .gitignore excludes session_plan/, so the files are on disk but not in git. I didn't force-add them, assuming the harness reads them from disk.

Task 1 (product), Part of #1149: say in the docs that `-p` and piped yoyo approve every tool call. According to the assessment, non-interactive runs auto-approve everything, and only hard-deny and the user's deny list stop a call. The docs never say this, and permissions.md shows yoyo -y -p … as if -y were needed. The task touches only permissions.md, single-prompt.md and piped-mode.md, and it checks the cited code lines before writing anything. It doesn't change the default.

Task 2 (product), Part of #1114: `flag_value` skips a flag's value slot. The title repro (yoyo -p --print-system-prompt) has been fixed since Day 247. The assessment called it open because it read the issue body, not the comments. What's left is in the latest comment: yoyo --system --model claude-zzz -p hi runs on model claude-zzz. The task:
• counts every flag_value caller from grep, since they don't all pass argv in the same shape;
• fixes flag_value where it's defined, so every caller gets the fix;
• adds tests against the real binary, including a check that --model claude-zzz -p hi still selects that model, and a revert-and-restore run to prove the new test catches the bug;
• stays out of cli.rs, which is exactly at its recorded size cap.

Done at planning:
• Filed #1149, asking @yuanhao to choose between keeping auto-approve (my default, with the docs disclosure) and denying tools that aren't allowed unless --yes is passed. Choosing the second would break my own loop as it stands. scripts/evolve.sh (around line 744) pipes the prompt in on stdin with no --yes I could see, and that file is protected, so he would have to add the flag. I'm holding the default until he answers.
• Size-gate warning left for the next planner in issue_responses.md. help.rs is 10 lines from the size limit that fails cargo test, and commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 lines from it. Neither task touches them, but the next help.rs edit (probably a #1127 slice) has to deal with this in the same diff.
